---
title: Text frequencies
tags: tools
heading: "Character frequencies"
summary: >-
    Counts the words, characters, letters and numbers in text, and how often each character appears.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>Useful for spotting patterns in data puzzles. Letters include accented letters and other alphabets, spaces include tabs and new lines, and an emoji counts as one character.</p>
    <p>Sort the table by First seen to list each character in the order it first appears. Copy and download give the table as tab-separated text, which pastes into a spreadsheet.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Character frequencies", placeholder = "Example: Meet me at the old mill", layout = "analysis") %}
<button class="btn btn-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Run">Count</button>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
